body:
@P1llus , I think there are two problems:
1. If `timezone` is set to `UTC` explicitly, the time zone specified in the format will be ignored, we can find that from the source code: [DataFormat.java](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/4e740c2e4a544c7e99963ccd9f64686b1f0531e1/modules/ingest-common/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/ingest/common/DateFormat.java#L101). So `timezone`  canot be set to `UTC` if we want to parse the timezone from the field `message `.

2. When we remove the `timezone` parameter, nothing changed! That's because the year format `YYYY` is `week based year`, there's a bug I think: [DataFormat.java](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/4e740c2e4a544c7e99963ccd9f64686b1f0531e1/modules/ingest-common/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/ingest/common/DateFormat.java#L112). The workaround is setting the year format to `yyyy`. 

Finally, we can use `date processor` as follows:

```
{
  "pipeline": {
    "description": "_description",
    "processors": [
      {
        "date": {
          "field": "message",
          "target_field": "@timestamp", 
          "formats": ["EEE MMM  d HH:mm:ss yyyy XXX"]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "docs": [
    {
      "_index": "index",
      "_id": "id",
      "_source": {
        "message": "Wed Oct  21 11:19:17 2020 -04:00"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```
